        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent admission of your 83-year-old female patient, who presented to our department on 16/08/2007 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited significant dyspnoea, reduced oxygen saturation, and increased sputum production. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. She was promptly commenced on supplemental oxygen, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged on 17/08/2007 with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Pulmonary rehabilitation and COPD self-management education were initiated. Please arrange early follow-up.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
